Under "really stupid questions": you're running
MS-Windows XP, so why on earth are you rebuilding an
_MS-DOS_ version of NetHack with _DJGPP_?

There are perfectly good free tools (cygwin's gcc,
and mingw, for two) that would let you rebuild a
WinXP version instead, and if you have a real life
that must be catered to off and on, playing NetHack
in a window that can be pushed out of the way is
much more pleasant than is playing NetHack full
screen, which I assume is what you end up doing.

xanthian.

I'm not sure if this is what you want, or is
appropriate, but my "downloaded and installed with
no changes" MS-Windows XP binary version of NetHack
has the below as what seems to be the identifying
information for the build:

# Internal representation of what version of Nethack
# you've used most recently
# do not edit this entry.
Nethack version = 26

Almost certainly, though, you should communicate
privately with Alexis Manning at

                [hearse @ hotpop.com]

*before* using Hearse with your build _at all_, you
might break something on the Hearse end, or find
Hearsed files breaking something on your end, or
worst case, upload bones files to Hearse that when
downloaded to someone elses bones directory crash
the recipient's game with a "trickery", if what you
think should be the identifying information for your
build turns out to be incorrect.




